$ jailops host show
SETTING       VALUE
hostname      fake-host
nameservers   198.51.100.1  /etc/resolv.conf
search        example.org
ntp servers   -  (the jailops block of /etc/ntp.conf)
ntpd          enabled
time          synchronised to 192.0.2.123

Managed:     no

JailOps does not change this host. To let it manage the identity, add to
/usr/local/etc/jailops/jailopsd.yaml:
  host:
    manage:
      modules: [identity]
and to /usr/local/etc/jailops/priv.conf:
  host-manage = identity
then: service jailops_priv restart && service jailopsd restart

$ jailops host identity set --hostname web1.example.org
! not_managed: JailOps does not manage the host's identity
! hint: add `host: {manage: {modules: [identity]}}` to jailopsd.yaml and `host-manage = identity` to priv.conf
[exit 3]

